    {
      "name": "EVENT_ISPACKETDONE",
      "file_offset": "0x10bacb4",
      "preferred_data_va": "0x14bb8b4"
    },
    {
      "name": "The Submit event submits one packet of source sample data to be played.",
      "file_offset": "0x10bacc8",
      "preferred_data_va": "0x14bb8c8"
    },
    {
      "name": "The Submit event is asynchronous and the submitted packet cannot be changed until the PacketPlayer has finished processing it. To determine when the packet has finished processing, use the EVENT_ISPACKETDONE event to query its state.",
      "file_offset": "0x10bad11",
      "preferred_data_va": "0x14bb911"
    },
    {
      "name": "This Stop event will stop all playback and remove all submitted packets from the internal queue.",
      "file_offset": "0x10bae28",
      "preferred_data_va": "0x14bba28"
    },
    {
      "name": "The Play event specifies format information about the source sample data that will be submitted andenters the PacketPlayer into an active state where submitted packets will start being processed.",
      "file_offset": "0x10baee8",
      "preferred_data_va": "0x14bbae8"
    },
    {
      "name": "The PacketPlayer event is asynchronous, meaning any output attributes the PacketPlayer supports will not be immediately updated to reflect the new state of the PacketPlayer.",
      "file_offset": "0x10bafad",
      "preferred_data_va": "0x14bbbad"
    },
    {
      "name": "The isPacketDone parameter is an output parameter used to indicate whether the specified packet has finished processing or not.",
